					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-694851#post-1851429</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-694851/scp-306#post-1851429</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 13 Sep 2013 18:59:59 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>IshmaelTibbs</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1697349</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This just doesn't grab me. It's decently written, but it just doesn't do it for me. I think part of it is that the central theme (the wart-toad connection) is a bit dull for me. It otherwise seems to be a bit all over a the place with warts really being viral, but here being fungal, and leading into amphibians. It just lacks the sort of coherance that makes it sound real and scary. Also, the whole frogs-with-human minds thing feels tacked on. They show little signs of remembering their former lives (minimizing the body horror of being trapped as a frog), and it downplays the infectious nature as the central concept.</p> <p>No vote for now. I need to mull it over more.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-694851#post-1851404</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-694851/scp-306#post-1851404</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 13 Sep 2013 18:10:50 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Communism will win</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>617958</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Nah. For one, that happens when everyone in your town is fucking fish-frogs and not from a fungus. Second, instead of morphing into a frog, the Innsmouthians start looking more and more like fish. Third, the story here's completely different &#8212; enough so that I didn't even make the connection myself.</p> <p>As for the article itself, I'm neutral on it.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-694851#post-1851280</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-694851/scp-306#post-1851280</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 13 Sep 2013 15:31:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>DrNietzsche</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1415487</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>If you're wondering, it's the process by which human-Deep One hybrids become more amphibious. They start out mostly human, but if they remain in Innsmouth, as they age past 20 or so, they start to become more and more like the Fish-Frog Deep Ones. Emphasis mostly on the frog bit, both in Lovecraft and here obviously. That's why I upvoted, because I love amphibians and body horror.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
